# Nissan Primera P12 four-door saloon, 2002-2007.
#
# The third Primera: a taller, more rounded car with the high-mounted badge, the
# narrow twin-blade grille and two swept-back lamp clusters that define its face.
# The saloon is modelled; the five-door liftback has a different rear end and is
# not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Primera
#
# Dimensions 4.565 x 1.760 x 1.480 m, wheelbase 2.704 m, from the English
# Wikipedia P12 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.913 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the P12 was located, so the objects carry
# plain colour names: silver, blue, red and black. Weights silver 3, black 2,
# blue 2, red 2, total 9, provisional pending the central rebase. The odd total
# is deliberate: this is a low-volume, fleet-heavy car and the weight is set a
# notch below its stablemates.
#
# Speed 190 km/h for the 1.6, the volume model. Comfort 100/330, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 100, a step above the P11. Classes 1,2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: March 2002 intro, retires staggered 2017-2020 on a
# thirteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-primera-p12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-primera-p12.dae (45 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-primera-p12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the bonnet and shoulders are more angular than the
# photographs and the rear lamp outlines are simplified. At 128 px the tall
# body, the swept lamp clusters and the divided grille read as the P12.

obj=citycar
name=NissanPrimeraP12(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2002
intro_month=3
retire_year=2020
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=330

